{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/480167-a-temporary-loss-of-willpower","id":480167,"title":"A temporary loss of willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T06:59:00-07:00","id":480167,"title":"A temporary loss of willpower","content":"So I was just looking at the Favored Form Merit, the drawback of which is that you lose a Mental of Physical Attribute dot for one of your forms. It specifically says this cuts all derived traits, too.<br /> My question, then, is what happens if you cut Resolve? You shift to that form, your Willpower pool is temporarily suppressed and you lose access to that top dot. When you shift up, do you get the point of Willpower back? Or is it just gone until you can regain it by normal means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T07:53:17-07:00","id":480231,"title":"","content":"I'd say you get it back, providing you had it in the first place and didn't spend willpower when shifted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:23:16-07:00","id":480402,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as far as I can remember the general rule is that the number of <i>spent</i> points remains constant whenever possible. But if it disappeared empty it comes back empty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}